  "sport": "soccer",
  "title": "The shadow",
  "description": "Players pair up with one ball per pair. The blue player dribbles and tries to shake off their shadow with turns, feints and changes of pace. The red shadow follows as closely as possible.\n\nWhen the coach calls \"Freeze!\" everyone stops. If the shadow is within arm's length the shadow wins, otherwise the player with the ball wins. Swap roles after each round.\n\nVariation: the shadow may try to win the ball. If the shadow wins it you swap roles at once. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Turn and change pace – sudden changes of speed are hardest to follow."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Use feints: pretend to go one way and go the other."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Look up so you don't run into the other pairs."
    }
  ],
